92186384801 1089 "q-126841" 13194139536126 true] [17592186384801 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536126 true] [17592186384801 1100 "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1),1-5t⟩$ at the point where $t=0,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" 13194139536126 true] [17592186384801 1113 #uuid "1276b48a-33df-5447-9033-1c8e5ee23a8f" 13194139536126 true] [17592186384801 1145 "At the point where $t=0,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(0)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(0)+u{r}^{′}(0),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({0}^{2}+1),1-5(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-5t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1},-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨\\frac{2(0)}{{0}^{2}+1},-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=0$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨0,1⟩+u⟨0,-5⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139536126 true] [17592186384802 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384803 13194139536126 true] [17592186384802 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384804 13194139536126 true] [17592186384802 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384805 13194139536126 true] [17592186384802 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384806 13194139536126 true] [17592186384802 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384807 13194139536126 true] [17592186384802 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536126 true] [17592186384802 1041 "selection" 13194139536126 true] [17592186384802 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384805 13194139536126 true] [17592186384802 1110 #uuid "b591f002-5937-58f1-80d8-406981dae9b0" 13194139536126 true] [17592186384803 1034 "⟨0,1⟩+u⟨2,0⟩" 13194139536126 true] [17592186384803 